<section>

    <h2>biography</h2>

    <p>
        Søren Kierkegaard was a Danish philosopher and writer whose
        work focused intensely on the individual, subjective
        experience, choice, faith and the difficulties of becoming
        oneself.
    </p>

    <p>
        His writings frequently examine anxiety, despair and the
        uncertainty that accompanies genuine choice. Rather than
        constructing philosophy as a detached system, Kierkegaard
        emphasized the lived experience of the individual and the
        responsibility of existing as a self.
    </p>

</section>


